<h2>Additional Resources</h2>
<p>For a concise overview of the history of Pennsylvania slavery and abolition, see Doug Harper's <a href="http://slavenorth.com/pennsylvania.htm">Slave North Project</a>.</p>
<p>For transcriptions of Pennsylvania's 1780 gradual abolition law in English and Spanish, see Yesenia Barragan's <a href="https://thefreewombproject.com/pennsylvania/">Free Womb Project</a>.</p>
<p>For a detailed accounting of sources pertaining to Pennsylvania slavery, see George Nagle's <a href="https://www.afrolumens.com/">AfroLumens Project</a>.</p>
<p>For a database of slavery records from several northern states, including Pennsylvania, see the <a href="https://nesri.commons.gc.cuny.edu/pennsylvania">Northeast Slavery Records Index</a>.</p>

